From: Ferrite overlay
Subject: [PATCH] std.posix: select std.os.ferrite for `system` on Ferrite

Wire `std.posix.system` to our `std.os.ferrite` namespace when the
overlay is active. That makes `std.posix.fd_t` resolve to our
ferrite-defined `fd_t` (u32, used as a slab-index handle by the Io
backend), which in turn makes `std.Io.Dir.Handle` and
`std.Io.File.Handle` come out as u32 without separate patches in
Io/Dir.zig and Io/File.zig.

Gate is `@hasDecl(std.os, "ferrite")` because nix-released Zig 0.16.0
still reports `native_os = .freestanding` for our builds; the compiler
binary doesn't recognize the `.ferrite` target string yet even though
Os.Tag lists it.

--- a/std/posix.zig
+++ b/std/posix.zig
@@ -34,7 +34,9 @@ const wasi = std.os.wasi;

 /// A libc-compatible API layer.
 pub const system = if (use_libc)
     std.c
+else if (@hasDecl(std.os, "ferrite"))
+    std.os.ferrite.system
 else switch (native_os) {
     .linux => linux,
     .plan9 => std.os.plan9,
